==Strategy==
==='''Chapters 1 & 2'''===
It is recommended to load up on [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] Uber Rares such as the [[Justice Strikes Back! Dark Heroes (Gacha Event)|Dark Heroes]] and [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]], as well as cats that can break Le'Solar's [[Barrier]] such as [[Skirt Cat (Special Cat)|Loincloth Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]]. It is far easier to bring Loincloth Cat or Crazed Bahamut Cat over Awakened Bahamut since Awakened Bahamut is essentially a one-shot attack - if A. Bahamut comes in as Le'Solar attacks, he will potentially die. Anyways, make sure to use good meatshielding strategies. [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] and whatever relevant Ubers will make the bulk of your offense.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The combination of a highly buffed Ursamajor and Le'Solar make beating this stage head on extremely difficult, especially since special and normal cats lack the usual alien counters. Instead, try to use the Gardeneel Bros. to your advantage by warping [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)| A.Bahamut]] past the alien backliners to destroy the enemy base using the money you get from killing the Celeboodle.

[[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] cannot survive a Ursamajor hit until Lv 50. If it's under levelled, you can use one or two defense combos, such as "[[Feel the Dance (Combo)|Feel the Dance]]" to better stall while A.bahamut destroys the base.

